{title: Who is Abimelech}
{subtitle: Judges 9:26; 9:28–29; 9:30–33; 9:35–38; 9:39–41}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 83}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | ×10
| [C] | [Dm] | [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Gaal son of Ebed came with his brothers [F]
[C]Moved into Shechem and stayed [Dm]
The leaders put their trust in him
In [C]the shadow of the city gate
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Who is A[Dm]bimelech and [F]who is Shechem
[C]That we should serve [Dm]him as our king
Is he [Bb]not the son of [Dm]Jerubbaal
With [C]Zebul as his deputy to [Dm]bring
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
At the temple of the god of Shechem [F]
[C]Gaal spoke his words of open defiance [Dm]
Serve the men of Hamor he said [F]
The [C]father of the city and its alliance
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Who is [Bb]Abimelech [F]and who is Shechem
[C]That we should serve [Dm]him as our king
Is he [Bb]not the son of [Dm]Jerubbaal
With [C]Zebul as his deputy to [Dm]bring
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]Zebul heard the words and anger [Dm]burned
[C]He sent messengers in the night [Dm]
[Bb]Lie in wait in the fields he whis[Dm]pered
[C]Strike at sunrise with your might
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm]Gaal stood at the gate and saw the troops [F]
[C]Coming down from the mountaintops [Dm]
Zebul mocked his vision of shad[F]ows
Saying you [C]see men where the earth is a stop
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [C] |
| [Dm] | [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Gaal fled before the chasing hand [Dm]
[C]Driven out from the place he had claimed
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [C] | [C] |
| [Dm] | [C] | [Dm] | [Dm] | ×2
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
